  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving Assistance to Displaced Populations in the Far-North Region of Cameroon through Shelter/Non-Food Items (NFI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Cameroon&#x2019;s Far-North region, ongoing hostilities and violence have heavily impacted local populations during the past five years, where displacements are still triggered due to small scale sporadic attacks by non-state armed groups as well as seasonal floods, other disasters and intercommunal tensions, underlying a great need in the region for the reinforcement of capacities to provide rapid humanitarian assistance. The overall objective of this project is to contribute to improve displaced populations&#x2019; well-being, dignity and save lives through the distribution of emergency and transitional shelter and non-food items (NFI) assistance in the three sub-divisions in the Far North region.</narrative>
  </description>
